{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1337338-running-a-game-for-my-kids","id":1337338,"title":"Running a game for my kids","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-22T10:48:26-07:00","id":1337338,"title":"Running a game for my kids","content":"I was thinking about running a table top RPG for my kids. I grew up in WW's D10 systems and had a ton of fun with them. I was going through all of the recent changes with Exalted and their combat system is a little intimidating to teach to my kids (pre-teens). They've expressed a lot of interest in magic and Mage seems like a decent system that's a decent entry into the CoD/WoD realms without requiring acknowledgement of the darker/brutaler themes present in other lines (particularly Vampire or Demon).<br /> <br /> From your perspective, how's Mage as an entry into tabletop gaming?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5706-zeal","name":"Zeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T12:30:14-07:00","id":1337347,"title":"","content":"You'll find plenty of advice for running for kids in <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/55727/World-of-Darkness-Innocents#targetText=The%20World%20of%20Darkness%20Through%20Innocent%20Eyes&amp;targetText=They&#39;re%20under%20your%20bed,they%20have%20made%20for%20themselves.\" target=\"_blank\">World of Darkness: Innocents</a> (first edition supplement, as evidenced by the way the game was called), so some adapting would need to be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T12:35:24-07:00","id":1337351,"title":"","content":"Mage is probably the most complex of all the gamelines, mechanically, with the spellcasting system being rather finiky.<br /> <br /> My advice would be to use the supernatural merits in the core rulebook and Hurt Locker (and maybe the unofficial supplement Second Sight: Third Eye) as a way to play less complicated spellcasters until the kids get a better feel for the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T13:47:40-07:00","id":1337363,"title":"","content":"On the thematic level.... don't underestimate the darkness of Mage's less 'brutal' themes. In many ways it can be much harsher because it's about psychological factors. Mages are hubristic junkies, driven by arrogance and obsession. Mages are assholes, and being a &quot;nice&quot; mage isn't really good for your health.<br /> <br /> I would seriously consider Scion 2e for a younger audience unless they're explicitly expressing interest in the WoD/CofD already. Scion 2e is easier to work in young adult oriented tropes, all Hero level Scions have access to at least some form of magic on top of their specific powers (Purviews aren't that different from Arcana in concept even if much easier to get your head around: you get innate boosts/Attainments, individual powers in Boons/Rotes/etc., and the ability to be creative in applying them in Marvels or Creative Thaumaturgy).<br /> <br /> You're still going to get the d10 goodness, and there's plenty of experience they can build on if they express interest in something darker and you want to go to the CofD next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T19:07:30-07:00","id":1337417,"title":"","content":"Many adults have troubles with the spellcasting in this game. It would have to be simplified for kids, and I'm not really sure where to start. As people mentioned above, maybe it would be better to play with people with supernatural Merits. I haven't read the unofficial update of Second Sight, but the first edition might give you some inspiration for how to play un-awakened thaumaturges.<br /> <br /> That being said, I think Chronicles of Darkness is a great choice of system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-22T19:48:19-07:00","id":1337426,"title":"","content":"Kids are usually pretty smart. If they're down for being challenged give them Mage if that's what you want to do. Just be patient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}